# Tauri v2 Standards for Portly

- Use Tauri v2 plugin architecture and modular command handlers.
- Strongly type all IPC commands between Rust and React using Serde and TypeScript interfaces.
- Handle application lifecycle gracefully: background tray vs window closure.
- Do not block the Tauri main thread: run heavy socket scanning asynchronously using Tokio tasks.
- For privilege elevation, launch background helper commands via OS-specific mechanisms (`pkexec` on Linux, UAC on Windows).
